## Why This Is Asked

Explores cross-device, privacy-preserving data sharing with consent governance—an area not covered by existing questions. It tests ability to model costs across crypto, ledger, and data transfer, and to define actionable go/no-go criteria.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end encryption with device-scoped keys
- Consent ledger design and revocation propagation
- Cross-platform identity binding and offline considerations
- Cost drivers: hardware-backed storage, crypto ops, data transfer, regulatory penalties

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal consent ledger entry model
type LedgerEntry = {
  id: string;
  userId: string;
  deviceId: string;
  permissions: string[];
  revokedAt?: string;
  createdAt: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure revocation propagation latency across devices?
- What mitigations exist if a device is offline during revocation?

